/**
 * NASA.gov — Homepage Block Same-Background Adjacency Collapse
 * ============================================================
 * JIRA:   WWPTL-15, WWPTL-16, WWPTL-17
 *
 * Works with homepage-blocks.css.
 *
 * PROBLEM
 * ───────
 * Every block has 4.5rem top + 4.5rem bottom padding.
 * When two adjacent blocks share the same background color, the
 * combined 9rem gap looks doubled. We collapse it to 4.5rem by zeroing
 * the top padding of the second block via .hp-collapse-top.
 *
 * WHY JS
 * ──────
 * CSS cannot inspect a sibling's computed background color.
 * Block order and color mode are both editable in the CMS —
 * hardcoded sibling selectors break the moment an editor reorders
